    "content": "The Dallas Wings selected UConn guard Azzi Fudd with the No. 1 overall pick in the 2026 WNBA Draft. The draft featured expansion teams Toronto Tempo and Portland Fire, with UCLA setting a record by having five players selected in the first round, including Lauren Betts (No. 4) and Gabriela Jaquez (No. 5).2026 WNBA First Round Draft OrderDallas Wings: Azzi Fudd (UConn)Minnesota Lynx (via Chicago): Olivia Miles (TCU)Seattle Storm (via LA Sparks): Awa Fam Thiam (Spain)Washington Mystics: Lauren Betts (UCLA)Chicago Sky (via Connecticut): Gabriela Jaquez (UCLA)Toronto Tempo: Kiki Rice (UCLA)Portland Fire: Iyana Martín Carrión (Perfumerias Avenida)Golden State Valkyries: Flau'jae Johnson (LSU - traded to Seattle)Washington Mystics (via Seattle): Angela Dugalić (UCLA)Indiana Fever: Raven Johnson (South Carolina)Washington Mystics (via NY Liberty): Cotie McMahon (Ole Miss)Connecticut Sun (via Phoenix): Nell Angloma (Lattes Montpellier)Atlanta Dream: Madina Okot (South Carolina)Seattle Storm (via Las Vegas): Taina Mair (Duke)Connecticut Sun (via Minnesota): Gianna Kneepkens (UCLA)Key NotesExpansion Teams: Toronto Tempo and Portland Fire made their inaugural draft picks.UCLA Dominance: UCLA had a historic night with five first-round picks: Lauren Betts, Gabriela Jaquez, Kiki Rice, Angela Dugalić, and Gianna Kneepkens.Top Picks: Following Fudd, TCU's Olivia Miles went second, and Spain's Awa Fam Thiam went third.",
